# Path to your local checkout of ios-consumer-app.
# App configs are read from "$CONSUMER_APP_DIR/Apps" (config.xcconfig,
# GoogleService-Info.plist, Assets/) and applied back into this same checkout.
#
# Leave it empty to auto-detect a sibling checkout (../ios-consumer-app), which is
# all a fresh clone of this repo needs.
CONSUMER_APP_DIR="/Users/ashutoshsingh/Desktop/work/ios-consumer-app"

# ── screenshots.sh (all optional — these are the defaults) ──
# Branch the screenshot run checks out and pulls before building.
# SCREENSHOT_BRANCH="development"
# Simulators for the two App Store slots: 6.5" and 13". If you don't have these,
# the script offers to create them; run './screenshots.sh --check' to see where you
# stand, and 'xcrun simctl list devices available' for what you already have.
# SCREENSHOT_IPHONE_DEVICE="iPhone 14 Plus"
# SCREENSHOT_IPAD_DEVICE="iPad Pro 13-inch (M5)"
# Where <AppName>_Screenshots gets created.
# SCREENSHOT_OUTPUT_ROOT="$HOME/Desktop"
# Freeze the status bar at 9:41, full bars, full battery.
# SCREENSHOT_CLEAN_STATUS_BAR="true"
# Products added before the cart shot (a target, not a guarantee).
# SCREENSHOT_CART_ITEMS="3"
# true → also stream every tap and keystroke. Off by default; the step-by-step
# narrative plus failures is enough to follow a run, and the full xcodebuild log is
# always written to $TMPDIR/consumer-screenshots-<slot>.log.
# SCREENSHOT_VERBOSE="false"
# Hard ceiling on the UI test, in seconds. A screen it can't reach can never hang
# the run — XCTest kills the test and the shots taken so far still come back.
# SCREENSHOT_TEST_TIMEOUT="1500"